# The Development Workflow

This repository uses `main` as the default branch. Never commit to `main`:
branch from an up-to-date `main`, open a PR, let CI decide.

## The loop

1. **Plan.** Read `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc`;
   check the open PRs so the change does not cross someone else's.
2. **Implement** on a feature branch. Keep the README tool table and the tests
   in step when a tool changes.
3. **Verify locally** with what CI runs:
   - `make test` (unit), `make lint`, `make fmt`;
   - `pre-commit run --all-files` — gofmt, goimports (`-local
     github.com/giantswarm/mcp-template`), golangci-lint with gosec/goconst,
     `go mod tidy`, the values schema;
   - `make helm-lint`, `make helm-template`, `make helm-test` for chart changes;
   - `make govulncheck` when dependencies move.
4. **PR** with a Conventional Commit title (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`,
   `feat!:` for a breaking change) — the title becomes the release note.
5. **Release** happens on merge when the repo's team file has
   `ci.generate: true`: the Auto Release workflow tags `main` (git-cliff
   decides the bump from the commit type; `docs:` releases nothing), and the
   CircleCI tag pipeline publishes the multi-arch image, the chart and — with
   the `cli` flavour — the six platform binaries with their cosign bundles.

## Generated files

`.circleci/*`, `Makefile`, `Makefile.gen.*.mk`, `.pre-commit-config.yaml`,
`renovate.json5`, `.nancy-ignore.generated` and every `zz_generated.*` file
are written by devctl from the team file in giantswarm/github
(`repositories/<team>.yaml`) and kept in sync by the align-files workflow.
Change them there, never here; repo-specific configuration goes to
`Makefile.custom.mk`, `.circleci/custom.yml`, `renovate-custom.json5`.

## Versioning

`pkg/project` is the only version source: the generated Makefile and the
architect `go-build` job stamp `version`, `gitSHA` and `buildTimestamp` with
`-ldflags -X`; a plain `go build` falls back to Go's VCS build info. Do not
add version variables elsewhere — `mcp-template version`, `--version`,
the MCP server info and `self-update` all read `rootCmd.Version`.
`self-update` only works for repos with the `cli` flavour (release binaries
and their cosign bundles); without it every release is refused as unsigned.
